    8:{"science":"The parts of an insect’s body, how they move, what size they are and what each part is for; what they eat and where they live.", "math":"Counting legs, wings and parts; comparing sizes with a ruler.", "comunicacion":"The labelled diagram: writing the name of each part in the right place.", "english":"It has got six legs. These are the wings. It eats leaves.", "art":"Large-scale diagram for the classroom wall.", "social":"Where they live in the school: map of the places where they turn up.", "music":"Rhythms in six beats, like six legs.", "pe":"Game of imitating insect movements.", "tutoria":"What frightens me and why; talking about it as a group."},
