    5:{"math":"Tally chart, which is what Maths gives these two weeks. Always counting at the same time of day.", "science":"Recording the figure on the spot and not from memory.", "comunicacion":"Writing down the date, the time and the place of each count.", "social":"Comparing my area with a classmate’s.", "english":"I saw six bottles. There are more on Monday.", "art":"Designing the record sheet.", "pe":"Daily consistency: the count is done every single day.", "tutoria":"Keeping a five-day commitment."},
    6:{"math":"The same figures as a bar chart and as a pictogram with a scale up to 10; which is easier to understand and why.", "comunicacion":"Giving the chart a title and writing one sentence with the finding.", "science":"What the chart says that the table did not.", "social":"What we would do with that figure if we were the school.", "english":"On Monday there were six. Friday was the worst day.", "art":"The chart, large, for the wall.", "music":"Counting song using the pictogram scale.", "tutoria":"Showing my chart to someone else and listening to what they understand."},
